No, look, the way I'm cutting it is a bit...

571
00:19:47,780 --> 00:19:48,740
It's fine, you eat first.

572
00:19:48,740 --> 00:19:50,140
Whatever you leave is my bite.

573
00:19:51,260 --> 00:19:52,340
Okay.

574
00:19:54,540 --> 00:19:55,700
The milky taste is a bit strong.

575
00:19:57,300 --> 00:19:57,900
You eat this side.

576
00:19:57,900 --> 00:19:58,940
Start eating from this side.

577
00:19:59,340 --> 00:20:00,580
Eat the part that hasn't soaked in the milk.

578
00:20:01,540 --> 00:20:05,220
Leave the milky part for me.

579
00:20:08,420 --> 00:20:09,340
Sometimes when I taste milk

580
00:20:09,340 --> 00:20:10,460
I suddenly feel nauseous.

581
00:20:10,740 --> 00:20:11,420
Me too.

582
00:20:11,900 --> 00:20:13,180
Yogurt is fine though.

583
00:20:13,180 --> 00:20:14,460
I really love drinking yogurt.

584
00:20:19,420 --> 00:20:20,500
This is just too good.

585
00:20:21,940 --> 00:20:22,820
It feels sinful.

586
00:20:23,300 --> 00:20:24,700
In the past, this was

587
00:20:25,300 --> 00:20:26,300
something I would never eat.

588
00:20:26,300 --> 00:20:27,180
Yeah.

589
00:20:27,620 --> 00:20:29,740
But I still want to take you

590
00:20:30,460 --> 00:20:32,340
to see some good stuff. Why

591
00:20:33,660 --> 00:20:34,740
are you holding me back?

592
00:20:34,740 --> 00:20:36,140
See some good stuff? What do you mean?

593
00:20:36,580 --> 00:20:37,540
Take me to eat more

594
00:20:37,540 --> 00:20:39,300
like Hainanese chicken rice and things like that, right?

595
00:20:39,780 --> 00:20:42,060
Let me show you the beauty of our country.

596
00:20:43,060 --> 00:20:44,860
When I used to travel for work,

597
00:20:44,860 --> 00:20:47,260
I really discovered a lot of cities with great food.

598
00:20:47,700 --> 00:20:49,020
Which city do you like the most now?

599
00:20:49,020 --> 00:20:50,820
I like coastal cities and islands.

600
00:20:50,820 --> 00:20:52,060
Then you haven't been to Qingdao.

601
00:20:52,060 --> 00:20:52,780
That's a bit of a shame.

602
00:20:52,780 --> 00:20:54,740
But I like places like Hainan.

603
00:20:56,060 --> 00:20:58,740
Actually, summer in Qingdao

604
00:20:59,260 --> 00:21:00,580
is more fun than summer in Hainan.

605
00:21:01,620 --> 00:21:03,860
Actually, a lot of my friends are from Qingdao.

606
00:21:03,860 --> 00:21:04,460
They keep inviting me to visit.

607
00:21:04,460 --> 00:21:05,980
But I still haven't been there.

608
00:21:05,980 --> 00:21:07,060
Several friends.

609
00:21:08,060 --> 00:21:10,180
Do you want to consider

610
00:21:11,180 --> 00:21:12,540
going there during your annual leave?

611
00:21:14,740 --> 00:21:15,980
We can make some plans.

612
00:21:19,900 --> 00:21:20,940
But if you're living alone now,

613
00:21:20,940 --> 00:21:22,060
you could get a kitten or something.

614
00:21:23,660 --> 00:21:24,460
I wouldn't be able to take care of it.

615
00:21:24,820 --> 00:21:26,140
I think it's really not suitable for someone alone

616
00:21:26,140 --> 00:21:26,940
to have a pet.

617
00:21:26,940 --> 00:21:28,060
No matter what your situation is,

618
00:21:28,060 --> 00:21:29,980
you need to have a backup at home.

619
00:21:30,860 --> 00:21:32,100
Whether it's a cat or a dog,

620
00:21:33,420 --> 00:21:36,740
the backup is ready to step in.

621
00:21:40,740 --> 00:21:41,700
What time is it now?

622
00:21:42,580 --> 00:21:43,580
Actually, we can head back now.

623
00:21:43,940 --> 00:21:45,420
Okay, I'll give it a try.

624
00:21:46,460 --> 00:21:47,620
But your hands are too cold.

625
00:21:48,740 --> 00:21:49,060
Yeah.

626
00:21:49,700 --> 00:21:51,620
You're really cold. Are you wearing enough clothes?

627
00:21:52,100 --> 00:21:54,260
Your hands are cold because you're cold.

628
00:21:54,260 --> 00:21:54,900
Okay.

629
00:21:55,260 --> 00:21:55,940
Let's go.

630
00:22:07,260 --> 00:22:08,420
Where should I stick this?

631
00:22:09,820 --> 00:22:11,300
It seems like there's nowhere left to stick it.

632
00:22:11,300 --> 00:22:12,460
Stick it on the sleeve.

633
00:22:12,780 --> 00:22:13,940
Stick it on your lower abdomen.

634
00:22:14,420 --> 00:22:16,260
Can you stick it on your long johns? Is that okay?

635
00:22:16,260 --> 00:22:17,100
No need to stick any more.

636
00:22:17,100 --> 00:22:18,260
It's fine, just leave it like this.

637
00:22:19,100 --> 00:22:21,060
Thinking about it, today must be really tough.

638
00:22:22,620 --> 00:22:24,820
Open two more, give me your legs.

639
00:22:26,820 --> 00:22:27,780
Stick it on your calves.

640
00:22:32,900 --> 00:22:34,380
You should put on a mask.

641
00:22:34,740 --> 00:22:35,740
Never mind, I'll wear it.

642
00:22:36,100 --> 00:22:37,500
No, let me wear it.

643
00:22:37,500 --> 00:22:38,620
Everyone is wearing a mask.

644
00:22:38,620 --> 00:22:39,620
You don't have to wear it, okay?

645
00:22:39,980 --> 00:22:42,060
This way you can sleep better, okay?

646
00:22:42,060 --> 00:22:43,700
It's fine, I've already put it on.

647
00:22:58,900 --> 00:23:00,820
The weather is amazing today.

648
00:23:03,380 --> 00:23:04,740
Let's go!

649
00:23:06,100 --> 00:23:07,180
Which way?

650
00:23:08,060 --> 00:23:08,620
This way.

651
00:23:09,300 --> 00:23:10,300
It's so cold.

652
00:23:12,940 --> 00:23:14,860
There seems to be a place up ahead.

653
00:23:16,980 --> 00:23:18,140
Is there finally a spot?

654
00:23:32,700 --> 00:23:33,620
So warm.

655
00:23:35,140 --> 00:23:36,860
There's a tea stove here.

656
00:23:37,940 --> 00:23:39,500
It's already burning.

657
00:23:39,780 --> 00:23:40,660
That's great.

658
00:23:40,660 --> 00:23:41,460
So comfortable.

659
00:23:41,460 --> 00:23:43,140
We have this every day.

660
00:23:44,580 --> 00:23:45,980
It doesn't seem very hot yet.

661
00:23:47,220 --> 00:23:48,620
I'll get two more cups of water.

662
00:23:52,860 --> 00:23:53,540
It's hot.

663
00:24:07,380 --> 00:24:08,660
Thank you.

664
00:24:16,700 --> 00:24:18,500
What were you planning to do today?

665
00:24:18,500 --> 00:24:19,380
I don't know.

666
00:24:20,340 --> 00:24:21,660
I didn't have any special plans.

667
00:24:22,020 --> 00:24:23,300
I was just thinking about what everyone else had planned.

668
00:24:23,300 --> 00:24:24,500
Just go along with everyone.

669
00:24:28,180 --> 00:24:29,180
Thank you.

670
00:24:31,620 --> 00:24:32,580
Thank you.

671
00:24:38,740 --> 00:24:41,780
You're actually quite outgoing.

672
00:24:42,140 --> 00:24:43,140
I'm outgoing.

673
00:24:47,700 --> 00:24:49,380
Then you're an introvert.

674
00:24:49,380 --> 00:24:50,860
I guess I'm an introvert.

675
00:24:51,420 --> 00:24:52,140
You're an extrovert.

676
00:24:54,060 --> 00:24:55,260
But I really am.

677
00:24:55,940 --> 00:24:57,620
The most introverted among extroverts.

678
00:24:58,100 --> 00:24:59,380
The most introverted person.

679
00:25:14,460 --> 00:25:15,060
Thank you.

680
00:25:30,660 --> 00:25:32,300
So do you prefer someone more outgoing

681
00:25:32,300 --> 00:25:33,380
or someone more introverted?

682
00:25:34,580 --> 00:25:35,460
Probably outgoing.

683
00:25:37,260 --> 00:25:38,940
There really are outgoing people.

684
00:25:40,500 --> 00:25:42,100
I think being with someone outgoing

685
00:25:42,100 --> 00:25:43,500
might be a bit easier.

686
00:25:43,900 --> 00:25:44,540
Yeah.

687
00:25:44,540 --> 00:25:45,020
Right?

688
00:25:45,020 --> 00:25:45,620
True.

689
00:25:59,580 --> 00:26:01,420
Were there any interesting stories after the show aired?

690
00:26:01,420 --> 00:26:02,660
What about season four of "Half-mature Lovers"?

691
00:26:02,660 --> 00:26:03,860
Left hand, ceiling level.

692
00:26:03,860 --> 00:26:04,700
Right hand.

693
00:26:05,700 --> 00:26:06,700
That's amazing.

694
00:26:08,300 --> 00:26:10,220
What's with that expression?

695
00:26:10,220 --> 00:26:12,180
Why would I say something like that?

696
00:26:12,180 --> 00:26:14,340
Help, Teacher Hou!

697
00:26:14,340 --> 00:26:16,100
When I saw these letters from Xiao Hou,

698
00:26:16,100 --> 00:26:17,140
I was really touched.

699
00:26:17,140 --> 00:26:18,300
Xiao Hou is really gentle.

700
00:26:19,660 --> 00:26:20,980
You two have gotten this far in your conversations?

701
00:26:21,420 --> 00:26:22,620
From my god's-eye view,

702
00:26:23,020 --> 00:26:26,140
This is so sweet, bro, just a little bit.

703
00:26:26,140 --> 00:26:28,140
It's for you, bro.

704
00:26:28,140 --> 00:26:29,460
I think my facial expressions

705
00:26:29,460 --> 00:26:31,540
still need improvement, it's not good enough.
